<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tui</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tuy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tui is a town in the province of Pontevedra in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a>, on the Miño river opposite Valença in Portugal. A Roman town and the seat of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> from the sixth century, it was destroyed in the Muslim conquest and resettled under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ordono-i-of-asturias">Ordoño I of Asturias</a> in the ninth century. Its fortified cathedral, begun in the twelfth century, overlooks the river border.</p></div>
